{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And Moses wrote their goings out, etc.</b> One needs to know what the verse informs us in this statement — if to say that Moses wrote them, is not the entire Torah written by Moses, and the journeys written in the Torah included within the Torah? Further, it should have said ״וַיִּכְתֹּב מֹשֶׁה אֶת מַסְעֵיהֶם״. Further, why did it repeat saying <b>and these are their journeys</b>, etc., when it has already said ״אֵלֶּה מַסְעֵי״ etc.? Further, why did it change: at first it prefaced saying <b>their goings out</b> and afterward said <b>their journeys</b>, and afterward it prefaced the word <b>their journeys</b> before the word <b>their goings out</b>?" "<b>And it appears</b> that the verse intends to inform us of the order of the writing of the journeys — that they were not written on a single day, but rather according to this order: that Moses began to write in his register by command of the King from the day they left Egypt in this manner — on the day they left Egypt he wrote the verse ״וַיִּסְעוּ בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל מֵרַעְמְסֵס״ etc., the two verses that appear together before us up to the word ״שְׁפָטִים״; and when they encamped in Sukkot he wrote the verse ״וַיִּסְעוּ וְגוֹ׳ וַיַּחֲנוּ בְּסֻכּוֹת״; and when they journeyed from Sukkot he wrote ״וַיִּסְעוּ מִסֻּכּוֹת״; and when they encamped in Eitam he wrote ״וַיַּחֲנוּ בְּאֵיתָם״; and so in this manner he would write each journey in its time until they reached the plains of Moav. And afterward HaShem said to him that he should arrange them in the Torah in the order they were written in his possession, and this is what the verse says <b>and Moses wrote their goings out</b> — meaning the day they left Egypt, namely the two verses from ״וַיִּסְעוּ מֵרַעְמְסֵס״ to the word ״שְׁפָטִים״. And His saying <b>their journeys</b> — meaning the order of all their journeys that they traveled from the day of their going out from Egypt until the end of the journeys. And His saying <b>by the mouth of HaShem</b> — to say that even the initial writing itself was by the mouth of HaShem; He told him that he should keep writing as they went. And His saying <b>and these are their journeys</b> etc. — meaning, these are the journeys spoken of that Moses wrote <b>for their goings out</b>, each one in its time and place, and this is the transcription."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:17:05.603328070Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}